ich of course drake would  like to do props to apu for still  laughing and seeming fine after  everything he's been through including  being cut down by zorro he's definitely  worthy of the supernova title yeah he's  not moral but pirates don't have to be  and the fact that he's talking about  backstabbing ianko here means he's more  strategic than hawkins was at least for  instance hawkins didn't have to fight  killer at all if he was just looking  after himself again we can't be sure  that he won't just backstab drake if  kaido ends up being fine but he's  definitely convincing when he's speaking  to drake saying no matter how this war  ends the winner isn't going to come out  unscathed they'll be easy pickings he  ambitiously suggests teaming up with  drake and swooping in and stealing  victory at the last moment he makes a  lot of sense when he says neither of  them have a horse in this race and thus  there's no point for them to go at it  and after the way queen treated up who  it's not surprising that he would turn  on that unappreciative crew as soon as  he got the chance obviously drake has  trouble trusting him but apu points out  trusting has nothing to do with it since  the arrangement will be mutually  beneficial for both of them adding that  this is a once in a lifetime opportunity  and appu is right even if drake doesn't  want to team up with him as a member of  the marines it doesn't make sense for  him to risk fighting a poo in these  numbers to the end when they're not  getting in his way and kaido is  obviously the bigger catch depending on  what he chooses to do we'll learn more  about drake's character and sense of  principles for sure i really look  forward to seeing how apu's plans pan  out in no world do i see him swooping in  and getting full credit for defeating  kaido and the straw hats but if he teams  up with powerful enough allies like  blackbeard perhaps who knows either way  he's a slippery dude and seemingly has a  way out whatever happens if kaido wins  he could keep pretending to be on his  side if he loses and the marines come  he'll hopefully have an understanding  with undercover marine drake he  definitely makes for an interesting  antagonist at this point we then see  hamlet carrying komachiyo to safety down  the stairs while usopp and nami spot  kinemon's detached legs begging for help  this is an interesting throwback to punk  hazard to be sure and it's hilarious how  they first mistake the legs for a  torso-less yokai usop hugs the legs  which in and of itself looks hilarious  and tells the legs that are looking for  some allies that he's an ally although  of course legs don't have ears and can't  hear so kinemon is clearly alive but  usopp does comment on how much he's  bleeding and yeah it is fitting that  kinemon gets to see the kind of man momo  becomes since the legs can't hear nami  draws the crescent mark of the rebellion  on him with her fingers and he realizes  based on this that they are allies the  legs request help and usopp rushes over  on hamlet who just looks so funny as he  moves around we find out that kinemon is  searching for help for kiku kiku is  barely clinging to life and needs to be  saved asap so even kiku is still alive  but it's not that surprising since one  piece is infamous for not killing off  characters after it's implied that they  may have died not that it never happens  but it usually never happens then there  are more character survivals kinemon  overhears orochi calling out to kanjur  kinemon thought orochi is dead so he's  surprised and he thinks that orochi is  unaware of kundro's demise but insanely  kanjuro is still kicking this guy just  won't die oda decided to jam pack all  these still alive moments in one chapter  and i guess by doing so we won't have a  bunch of chapters with one person  popping up revealing they're still alive  this way he gets a lot of them out of  the way at once and we can focus on  other aspects over the upcoming chapters  so kanjuro is on the brink of death but  still not dead and don't for a second  assume that he'll stop causing trouble  just because he's on the brink of death  oh no orochi gets him to paint the  burning wrath of the kurozumi clan with  the last strength he has left he tells  kundro free their souls and free us in a  final blaze of glory so kundrov views it  as a kurozumi pact and creates the giant  fire creature called kazembo this keeps  the yokai aspect alive as kazimbo is a  type of yokai and it's very fitting if  you ask me because this type of yokai is  associated with monks who were still  attached to life on earth and were thus  considered failed buddhas they appeared  in the form of a mysterious fiery  apparition and as we know kundra was  very attached to the material world and  couldn't even let go of old grudges  deciding to hurt betray and even kill  people who viewed him as a friend  because of them the fire that represents  the vengeance of the kurozumi definitely  looks huge and burns people it touches  as well as its surroundings it can even  travel through walls like some kind of  ghost and you obviously can't shoot it  dead as some people try to do in the  meantime momo is still trying to create  the flame clouds and panicking it  doesn't help matters that now a new fire  is spreading everywhere and the castle  is being choked by flames brook just  tells robin to run from the flames  because there's no time to fight we get  some great shots reminding us of all the  forces in play including cp 0 the  samurai marco we also see a great half  page of luffy zorro and sanji's fight  side by side the straw hat monster trio  versus the beast pirates monster trio  and seeing that was definitely a treat  hard to believe we've come this far  already orochi says the kuzuki forces  and emperors will be undone by their own  hubris aka pride he's just laughing as  they fight knowing about the weapon  stockpiled in the basement and how the  fire will reach it soon and i said that  momo would succeed in his flame clouds  mission but there would have to be  another reason that yamato went to deal  with these stockpiled weapons anyways  and here is a possible reason even if  momo is a smashing success she'll have  to get rid of the weapons before the  flames spread there luckily being an  ice-based japanese wolf deity should  give her the best chance of stopping  slowing down a yokai fire orochi also  lied to kanjuro about the pact for them  to die with the rest of them because  he's waiting for fukurokuju so they can  escape together saying this pirate war  is no longer any of our business man it  will be so satisfying when this dude  gets his just desserts just saying and  it goes to show how op mythical zones  are even this week coward could survive  so many otherwise lethal attacks because  of his hydra like power i gotta say i  love seeing yamato's giant wolf form  running through the scene it would be so  useful and cool to have someone like  this around on the crew hashtag yamato  for straw hat she reaffirms to us that  momo will have to slow the island down  even if a bit so she can get to the  weapons at the bottom of the castle and  deal with them then we jump to the most  hyped part of the chapter big mom  fighting kid and law and using insane  attacks like ikoku sovereignty big mom's  really going at it and then we get a bit  of a flashback of kid and law talking  before this moment kid asks law if he  can awaken his ability and law says he's  not used to it yet he'd only use it if  they were near death since it burns too  much energy to use in real battle and  kid says his the same but they're not  getting anywhere without it and although  obviously there are drawbacks to using  the powers all i heard and got hyped  over was the fact that they both have  awakened abilities so they decide to  play their ace cards which are their  awakened devil crew powers that is so  hype not one but two awakened supernova  abilities targeted towards a yonko no  less oda is amazing at making multiple  amazing fights happen simultaneously  although i obviously am hyped to see  more of zorro vs king and luffy versus  kaido and so on i am totally okay and  enthralled with this king and law versus  big mom in the meantime law uses the  move croom which likely refers to  chromium which is poisonous in the body  and is lethal if the dose is high enough  he coats his sword with it and stabs  through big mop he says the incision is  harmless in and of itself although it  looks crazy just stabbing a yonko  through the neck but as he explains the  croom influences the body in other ways  he then unleashes a shock wave and big  mom starts bleeding from the mouth big  mom seems upset but relatively fine  afterwards now the question is will this  move have lasting damage and effects on  big mom's body as the name suggests it  should in theory weaken her and slow her  down and even get worse as time passes  but again i'm not sure how anime logic  will play itself out in this instance  anyways for now big mom is mad and  distracted by law so it's kids time to  show his awakening he uses a sign to  make big mom become a magnet all weapons  are being drawn to her and even the  steel beams of the tower are being  ripped out then kid tells law to get him  out of there and la uses his power to  make big mom and kids switch places thus  big mom is supposedly crushed by all the  falling debris as kid screams out punk  crash it's funny how again law was  saying don't tell me what to do before  he followed kids instructions despite  how cool a lot is he always seems to be  the one who loses it when luffy or kid  gives him orders but wow what a chapter  we're told by the narrator that this is  the awakened power mentioned and again  wow did it ever look awesome i find it  hard to believe that big mom is down for  the count but either way hopefully the  combination attack and especially lost  chrome attack will have lasting effects  and damage on big mom giving them an  upper hand keep in mind though they  probably won't last long either because  of the drained energy they spoke about  earlier so it's really a race to see who  drops first but if law and kit awaken  their fruit powers then we can  definitely expect fifth emperor luffy's  awakening too the question is has he  already awakened and that's why he's  able to do so well against kaido one on  one or are we on the brink of seeing  this awakening from luffy it would make  sense in a shonen story to save luffy's  awakening for after we see laws and kids  and not to mention it would be way more  hype if we saw something new so i do  have hopes that we will see something  new from luffy like with law and kid  though it will probably drain a lot of  stamina and will thus intensify the  final conflict but yeah let me know your  thoughts on all this the chapter once  again was called the impermanence of all  things and we saw big mom get wrecked  pretty hard at the very least the attack  reaffirmed that big mom is not  invincible does anybody think that she's  actually down for the count or at least  that she'll be considerably weakened  when she gets up will we see luffy's  awakening soon in epic fashion if the  supernova could pull it off the  so-called fifth emperor should be able  to do it too finally let me know what  you thought of this chapter and what you  expect to see in the next chapter mvp  for me will be shared by kid in law this  time around absolutely amazing to see  their awakened powers and whether  temporarily or not they made a yonko  bleed and then brought her down in epic  fashion let me know if you agree or have  another mvp in mind but anyways that is  it for this one another great chapter  with great moments as far as i'm  concerned if you did enjoy this chapter  review you know what to do channel the  pirate king within and smash that like  button with no mercy remember smashing  that like button